<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maeatae</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 200</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Maeatae were a confederation of peoples in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonine-wall">Antonine Wall</a>, recorded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassius-dio">Cassius Dio</a> around 200 CE, when they and the Caledonians fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> and provoked the campaigns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus">Septimius Severus</a>. Their name may survive in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dumyat">Dumyat</a> hill near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stirling">Stirling</a>, and the Miathi defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aedan-mac-gabrain">Áedán mac Gabráin</a> in the sixth century are thought to have been their successors.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maeatae.jpg" alt="Maeatae" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Doug Lee · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:From_Dumyat_looking_towards_Grangemouth_(geograph_3766267).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…Áedán mac Gabráin, who according to Adomnán was ordained king by Columba, campaigned widely: the annals record his expedition to Orkney around 580 and a battle around 582 in Manann, either the Isle of Man or Manaw on the Forth, and Adomnán describes his battle against the <b>Miathi</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/dal-riata">Dal Riata · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The Picts were not newcomers but descendants of the Iron Age peoples whom earlier Roman writers had called the Caledonii and the <b>Maeatae</b>, and of other tribes named by Ptolemy, such as the Vacomagi and Taexali.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-picts">Kingdom of the Picts · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
